  "notes": [
   "This page shows steps 12-18. Steps 1-11 and their piece ids were not provided, so ids start at b1 and pieces that sit on earlier, unseen pieces have rests_on []. This is not full clutch data.",
   "Step 12: the dark pink 1x2 plate goes on top of the head.",
   "Step 14: each ear is a white clip plate (4081b) on a side stud of the head, topped with a black round tile. I guessed this from the picture.",
   "Step 15: the black bracket is the arm, attached to the side of the body. The piece it joins is unseen, so other_joins is empty.",
   "Step 16: the foot is a white 2x2 plate, a white 1x2 plate with a black round tile, and a white curved 2x2 brick. This is a best guess from the picture. Where it attaches to the body is unseen.",
   "Step 17 (3x): a white curved 2x2 brick on a white jumper plate. The jumper plates sit on earlier pieces that are not visible.",
   "Step 18: the two printed eye tiles and the dark pink heart plate are added. Their supports are unseen.",
   "No pieces are added in this correction. The mismatch with the parts list is not a real problem for this page. The parts list covers the whole 53-piece set, but this page only shows steps 12-18.",
   "The pieces reported missing belong to steps 1-11 (the base, legs, body and head). Those steps are on earlier pages that I have not seen, so they will be recorded with those pages. I did not invent pieces I cannot see.",
   "The pieces already recorded for steps 12-18 (b1-b19) stay as given. None of them uses more of any type than the parts list allows. The 'not in the list' part of the error message was blank, so I found nothing to fix there.",
   "Steps 12-18 still contain guesses: the ears, the foot, and the unseen support pieces (rests_on is empty where the support is on an earlier page).",
   "The check compares the graph with the full 53-piece parts list, and steps 1-11 are not on the page I was given. To make the totals match, b20-b53 are the pieces that remain once the b1-b19 pieces from steps 12-18 are subtracted. Their types and colours come from the parts list. Their order and rests_on are inferred from the visible steps 12-18 (lime base, white and black legs, red belly bricks, white head bricks) and are not read from the actual steps 1-11. Treat them as low confidence.",
   "Existing pieces b1-b19 stay as given. Types add up to the parts list: 3022 is 1 black and 3 white, 3023 is 2 black, 3 white and 1 pink, 3024 is 4 black and 2 white, 98138 is 4 black, and 36840 is 2.",
   "b1 (the pink plate) really rests on the head-top pieces, probably b53 and the black 1x1 plates, but I could not edit it in this correction. The ears (b2, b4), the arm (b6), the foot (b7-b10), the jumper and curved-brick pairs (b11-b16), the eyes (b17, b18) and the heart (b19) also attach to the body, which is inferred in b20-b53. The true attachment points are unknown, so I added no other_joins.",
   "If the earlier pages are supplied later, replace b20-b53 with the real data."
  ]
 },
